---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Studio - The Whetstone"
  description="Structural audit, counterargument generation, citation checking, and revision tracking for writers."
  canonicalPath="/creator"
>
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pt-20 pb-16">

    <nav class="mb-10">
      <a href="/" class="text-xs text-muted hover:text-ink transition-colors">← The Whetstone</a>
    </nav>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-muted mb-3">Studio</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-ink-strong leading-tight mb-4">
        Stress-test your arguments<br class="hidden sm:block" /> before your readers do.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Structural audit, counterargument generation, citation checking, evidence verification,
        and the philosophical commitments your draft operates within - all before you publish.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="mb-14 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
      <a
        href="/creator/studio"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-accent-support text-white text-sm font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-accent transition-colors"
      >
        Open the Studio
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" />
        </svg>
      </a>
      <a
        href="/pricing"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-ink border border-hairline rounded-lg hover:bg-paper transition-colors"
      >
        View pricing →
      </a>
    </section>

    <!-- What the studio returns - editorial layout -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-muted mb-8">What the engine analyses</h2>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0 border border-hairline rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
        <div class="p-6 border-b md:border-b-0 md:border-r border-hairline">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-muted mb-2">Structure</p>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">Argument skeleton</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
            Every claim rendered as numbered premises with inference rules. Modus ponens, categorical syllogism,
            inductive generalisation - the formal structure of what you're actually arguing, stripped of rhetoric.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 border-b border-hairline">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-muted mb-2">Critique</p>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">26 reasoning patterns + 8 rhetorical techniques</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
            From Ad Hominem to Motte-and-Bailey, Selection Bias to Presupposition Smuggling.
            Each flagged with verbatim quotes, severity, and confidence. Inline highlights show exactly where.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 border-b md:border-b-0 md:border-r border-hairline">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-muted mb-2">Opposition</p>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">Counterargument generation</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
            The 2-3 strongest objections a thoughtful opponent would deploy that your draft fails to engage with.
            Each with its own Toulmin structure - claim, grounds, warrant.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 border-b border-hairline">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-muted mb-2">Sources</p>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">Citation audit</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
            Every cited URL fetched and checked against the claim it's cited for.
            Well-cited, weakly-cited, mismatched, or uncited - before your readers check for you.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 md:border-r border-hairline">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-muted mb-2">Framework</p>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">Philosophical commitments</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
            The ethical, epistemic, political, and methodological framework your argument operates within -
            made visible so you can decide whether to defend it, soften it, or replace it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-muted mb-2">Evidence</p>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">Evidence-weighted likelihood</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
            For empirical claims, we search 200M+ academic papers via Semantic Scholar and assess
            scientific consensus. Value claims are identified as such - they don't get percentages.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Who it serves -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-muted mb-8">Who it serves</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-0 border border-hairline rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
        <div class="p-6 border-b sm:border-b-0 sm:border-r border-hairline">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">Students & academics</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
            Thesis structure, evidence quality, counterargument handling, citation integrity.
            The question is "is your argument sound?" - not "did you write this?"
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 border-b border-hairline">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">Journalists</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
            Source verification, counterargument coverage, warrant exposure.
            Solo or multi-seat for newsrooms.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 sm:border-r border-hairline">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">YouTubers & Substackers</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
            Pre-publish audit for essay and analysis content.
            Revision tracking shows what improved between drafts.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">Newsrooms</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
            Multi-seat workspace, shared document library, API access.{' '}
            <a href="mailto:daniel.livingstone44@gmail.com" class="text-accent-support hover:text-accent font-medium">Get in touch →</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Base>
